\# Threadline Commercial Signal Capture

\#\# Why this exists  
Organic content creates commercial signals across multiple surfaces that Threadline may not automatically observe. Capture them weekly so results, attribution and content learning do not depend on memory.

\#\# After every meaningful prospect/customer conversation  
\- Date:  
\- Prospect/customer segment:  
\- Offer discussed:  
\- What they wanted:  
\- Trigger / why now:  
\- Problem in their exact words:  
\- Objection(s) in their exact words:  
\- Misconception / question:  
\- Competitor or alternative mentioned:  
\- Proof they cared about:  
\- Why they bought / did not buy / deferred:  
\- CTA/content they mentioned seeing:  
\- Specific asset/content ID if known:  
\- First touch source/content if known:  
\- Last touch source/content if known:  
\- New content idea implied:  
\- New research question implied:  
\- Offer/positioning feedback:

\#\# Weekly client commercial-signal capture  
Ask the client to report only what Threadline cannot reliably see:  
\- content-referenced DMs/enquiries;  
\- booked calls attributed or influenced by content;  
\- qualified opportunities and estimated pipeline value;  
\- closed-won deals/revenue where content was a known touch;  
\- buyer statements such as “I saw your video/post on…”;  
\- sales-call objections/questions that should feed future content;  
\- relevant offline/referral conversations influenced by the founder’s content.

For every commercial signal store:  
\- client;  
\- date;  
\- signal type;  
\- person/company if appropriate;  
\- asset/content ID or source if known;  
\- value/pipeline/revenue amount if applicable;  
\- evidence source;  
\- MEASURED vs CLIENT-REPORTED;  
\- attribution class: DIRECTLY\_TRACKED / BUYER\_NAMED\_CLIENT\_ATTRIBUTED / MULTI\_TOUCH\_INFLUENCED / ASSOCIATED\_CORRELATED / QUALITATIVE\_ONLY;  
\- first touch and last touch when known;  
\- notes / exact buyer language.

\#\# Promotion rules  
Repeated language can become a research signal. A single anecdote remains an anecdote until corroborated. Never convert buyer-named influence or correlation into causal revenue attribution.  
